# 🔐 **1. What is FBAC (Feature-Based Access Control)?**

**FBAC = permissions based on specific features and actions inside the system.**  
Much more precise than RBAC (Role‑Based Access Control).

### **RBAC = “District Officer” can access the district dashboard**

### **FBAC = “District Officer may: approve requisition, view stock, NOT modify procurement rules”**

In large and sensitive supply chains (as the PDFs highlight for DPE)  —  
**feature-level restriction is critical to prevent misuse, fraud, or accidental errors.** [\[Inventory Software | PDF\]](https://mnithmde-my.sharepoint.com/personal/md_amanullah_mni_thm_de/Documents/Microsoft%20Copilot%20Chat%20Files/Inventory%20Software.pdf)

